{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the angels of Elohim encountered him.</b> Those mentioned at the beginning of the parashah, who were ascending and descending upon it. And this is what it means by ״as he saw them״ — that is, he recognized them, for he had already seen them. And so it is written in Ezekiel (Ezekiel 10:15): ״היא החיה אשר ראיתי וגו'״ — 'this is the living creature that I saw, etc.' And according to what it began with Jacob and said, ״he went on his way,״ it would have been fitting to say, ״and he encountered the angels of Elohim.״ But this was for the preeminence of Jacob — like a man who says, 'men encountered the king.' And this encounter was to guard him, in the manner said of the righteous (Psalms 91:11): ״כי מלאכיו יצוה לך לשמרך בכל דרכיך״ — 'for His angels He will command concerning you, to guard you in all your ways.' And they said in the Midrash: who is greater, the guardian or the guarded? You should say, the guarded — as it is said, ״לשמרך״ — 'to guard you.' ״על כפים ישאונך״ — 'they shall bear you on their palms' (Psalms 91:12): who is greater, the bearer or the borne? You should say, the borne. And so here too: who is greater, the encounterer or the encountered? You should say, the encountered. And so we find with Elisha, where it is written (II Kings 6:15): ״וישכם משרת איש האלהים לקום ויצא והנה חיל סובב את העיר וסוס ורכב ויאמר נערו אליו אהה אדוני איכה נעשה״ — 'and the minister of the man of Elohim arose early to get up and go out, and behold, a force surrounded the city, with horses and chariots; and his lad said to him, Alas, my master, what shall we do?' And it is written: ״ויאמר אל תירא כי רבים אשר אתנו מאשר אותם״ — 'and he said, Do not fear, for they who are with us are more than they who are with them' (II Kings 6:16). And it is written: ״ויפקח ה' את עיני הנער וירא והנה ההר מלא סוסים ורכב אש סביבות אלישע״ — 'and YHWH opened the eyes of the lad and he saw, and behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire all around Elisha' (II Kings 6:17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:59.421488374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}